###
# 10xCards REST API Test Requests
# Use with REST Client extension in VS Code
###

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================================
### FLASHCARD ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================================

### 1.1 List Flashcards - GET /api/flashcards
# Default pagination (page 1, limit 20)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards

### List Flashcards - with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards?page=1&limit=10

### List Flashcards - filter by source
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards?source=manual&limit=5

### List Flashcards - filter by generation_id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards?generation_id=1&limit=10

### List Flashcards - all filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards?page=1&limit=5&source=ai-full&generation_id=1

### 1.2 Get Single Flashcard - GET /api/flashcards/:id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1

### Get Single Flashcard - Non-existent (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/99999

### Get Single Flashcard - Invalid ID (should return 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/invalid

### 1.3 Create Manual Flashcard - POST /api/flashcards
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "What is the capital of France?",
  "back": "Paris is the capital of France, known for the Eiffel Tower and rich cultural heritage."
}

### Create Manual Flashcard - Invalid (front too long, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "This is a very long question that exceeds the 200 character limit. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam.",
  "back": "Answer"
}

### Create Manual Flashcard - Invalid (missing back, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "Question without back?"
}

### 1.4 Bulk Create Flashcards - POST /api/flashcards/bulk
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/bulk
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "generation_id": 1,
  "flashcards": [
    {
      "front": "What is TypeScript?",
      "back": "TypeScript is a strongly typed programming language that builds on JavaScript.",
      "source": "ai-full"
    },
    {
      "front": "What is Astro?",
      "back": "Astro is a web framework for building fast, content-focused websites.",
      "source": "ai-edited"
    }
  ]
}

### Bulk Create Flashcards - Invalid (generation not found, should return 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/bulk
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "generation_id": 99999,
  "flashcards": [
    {
      "front": "Test",
      "back": "Test",
      "source": "ai-full"
    }
  ]
}

### Bulk Create Flashcards - Invalid (too many flashcards, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/bulk
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "generation_id": 1,
  "flashcards": [
    {"front": "Q1", "back": "A1", "source": "ai-full"},
    {"front": "Q2", "back": "A2", "source": "ai-full"},
    {"front": "Q3", "back": "A3", "source": "ai-full"}
    // ... repeat 51 times (max is 50)
  ]
}

### 1.5 Update Flashcard - PATCH /api/flashcards/:id
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "What is the capital of France? (Updated)",
  "back": "Paris, the City of Light."
}

### Update Flashcard - Partial update (only front)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "Updated front only"
}

### Update Flashcard - Partial update (only back)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "back": "Updated back only"
}

### Update Flashcard - Invalid (no fields, should return 400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}

### Update Flashcard - Non-existent (should return 404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/99999
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "Updated"
}

### 1.6 Delete Flashcard - DELETE /api/flashcards/:id
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1

### Delete Flashcard - Non-existent (should return 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/99999

### Delete Flashcard - Invalid ID (should return 400)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/invalid

### ============================================================================
### AI GENERATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================================

### 2.1 Generate Flashcard Suggestions - POST /api/generations
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/generations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_text": "TypeScript is a strongly typed programming language that builds on JavaScript, giving you better tooling at any scale. TypeScript adds additional syntax to JavaScript to support a tighter integration with your editor. Catch errors early in your editor. TypeScript code converts to JavaScript, which runs anywhere JavaScript runs: In a browser, on Node.js or Deno and in your apps. TypeScript understands JavaScript and uses type inference to give you great tooling without additional code. TypeScript is a syntactic superset of JavaScript which adds static typing. This basically means that TypeScript adds syntax on top of JavaScript, allowing developers to add types. TypeScript being a superset of JavaScript means that it contains all of the functionality of JavaScript, and then some. If you have written JavaScript before, you already know most of TypeScript. All JavaScript code is valid TypeScript code. TypeScript compiles down to JavaScript and can run anywhere that JavaScript runs!"
}

### Generate Flashcards - With custom model
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/generations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_text": "React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. It was developed by Facebook and is maintained by Facebook and a community of individual developers and companies. React can be used as a base in the development of single-page or mobile applications. However, React is only concerned with state management and rendering that state to the DOM, so creating React applications usually requires the use of additional libraries for routing and certain client-side functionality. React creates an in-memory data-structure cache, computes the resulting differences, and then updates the browser's displayed DOM efficiently. This process is called reconciliation. This allows the programmer to write code as if the entire page is rendered on each change, while the React libraries only render subcomponents that actually change. React components implement a render() method that takes input data and returns what to display. This example uses JSX syntax which is similar to XML. Input data that is passed into the component can be accessed by render() via this.props.",
  "model": "openai/gpt-4o"
}

### Generate Flashcards - Invalid (text too short, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/generations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_text": "This text is too short to generate flashcards."
}

### Generate Flashcards - Invalid (text too long, should return 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/generations
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "source_text": "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet... [text longer than 10000 chars]"
}

### 2.2 List Generations - GET /api/generations
# Default pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations

### List Generations - With pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations?page=1&limit=5

### List Generations - Page 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations?page=2&limit=10

### 2.3 Get Generation Statistics - GET /api/generations/statistics
# All time statistics (default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations/statistics

### Get Generation Statistics - Last week
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations/statistics?period=week

### Get Generation Statistics - Last month
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations/statistics?period=month

### Get Generation Statistics - All time (explicit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations/statistics?period=all

### Get Generation Statistics - Invalid period (should return 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/generations/statistics?period=year

### ============================================================================
### ERROR CASES
### ============================================================================

### Invalid JSON (should return 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{invalid json}

### Invalid endpoint (should return 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/nonexistent

### Invalid method (should return 405)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/flashcards/1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "front": "Test"
}
